## Conclusion

This was an excellent challenge combining several layers of analysis:

* Web reconnaissance
* Service identification
* socketcand / SocketCAN
* CAN traffic analysis
* State-versus-command differentiation
* Rolling-code behavior
* Replay testing
* Concurrency testing
* Protocol reverse engineering
* Checksum recovery
* CAN-frame forgery

The most satisfying part was that the challenge could not be solved simply by changing the visible vehicle state.
It required understanding the actual command path and producing a frame that the simulated receiver accepted as a legitimate fresh key-fob command.

